    "expertNote": "# Form 1.1: Property, plant and equipment - Cost\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: ppe | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 1.1: Property, Plant and Equipment - Cost\n\n**Purpose**:  \nForm 1.1 is used to document the initial cost of property, plant, and equipment (PPE) for an audit client. It helps in establishing a baseline understanding of the PPE items before diving deeper into valuation and depreciation.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nThis form should be completed during the onboarding phase of the audit, typically at the beginning when you first gather information about the client's PPE. You would use it whenever you need to record or verify the cost of new acquisitions or existing assets.\n\n**Key Fields**:  \n1. **Asset Description**: Clearly describe each piece of equipment or property.\n2. **Purchase Date**: Record the exact date the asset was acquired.\n3. **Cost**: Enter the total cost, including any additional costs necessary to bring the asset to its intended use.\n4. **Source of Information**: Indicate where you obtained this information (e.g., invoices, client records).\n5. **Verification Status**: Note whether and how you verified the cost information.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:  \n1. **Omitting Details**: Forgetting to fill in all required fields can lead to incomplete data.\n2. **Incorrect Costs**: Entering incorrect or outdated costs can skew your audit findings.\n3. **Ignoring Verification**: Not verifying the source of the cost information can result in inaccurate records.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form is foundational and feeds into other forms that assess depreciation, impairment, and overall valuation of PPE. It ensures that you have accurate starting points for these subsequent analyses.\n\n**ISA Context**:  \nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form aligns with ISAs related to the understanding of an entity’s internal control over financial reporting (ISA 501) and the audit",
