    "expertNote": "# Form 10.1: Intangible assets - Cost\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 1 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 10.1: Intangible Assets - Cost\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 10.1 is used to document the initial assessment of intangible assets' costs during the onboarding phase of an audit. This form helps auditors understand and verify the recorded costs of intangible assets, ensuring they are properly recognized and valued.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nYou should complete this form early in the audit process, typically during the planning stage when you're gathering information about the client's financial statements. It’s crucial when there are significant changes or additions to intangible assets from the previous year.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Description of Intangible Assets**: Clearly describe each intangible asset.\n2. **Cost Details**: Record the initial cost and any subsequent adjustments.\n3. **Acquisition Date**: Note when each asset was acquired.\n4. **Amortization Period**: Specify the period over which the asset will be amortized.\n5. **Source of Information**: Identify where you obtained the information about the assets.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Omitting Detailed Descriptions**: Failing to provide a clear and detailed description can lead to misunderstandings later in the audit process.\n2. **Incorrect Cost Details**: Entering incorrect or outdated cost figures can result in inaccurate financial reporting.\n3. **Ignoring Source of Information**: Not documenting where information came from can compromise the audit trail.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into other forms that require detailed asset information, such as Form 10.2 (Intangible Assets - Amortization) and Form 10.3 (Impairment of Intangible Assets). It also depends on preliminary financial statements and client interviews to gather necessary data.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form align",
