    "expertNote": "# Form 10.2: Intangible assets - Amortisation and impairment\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 4 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 10.2\n**Title:** Intangible Assets - Amortisation and Impairment  \n**Type:** Worksheet  \n**Audit Phase:** Onboarding (Phase 1)  \n**Category:** General  \n**Procedures:** 1  \n**ISA References:** ISA 330, ISA 500\n\n#### Purpose:\nThis form helps auditors assess the proper amortization and impairment of intangible assets. It ensures that the company is correctly accounting for these long-term assets over time.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form during the initial onboarding phase when you are assessing the client's financial statements. You should fill it out if the entity has significant intangible assets, such as patents or goodwill.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Description of Intangible Assets**: Clearly list all intangible assets.\n2. **Amortization Method**: Specify the method used (e.g., straight-line) and ensure it aligns with accounting policies.\n3. **Impairment Testing Details**: Document how impairment is tested and when it was last performed.\n4. **Accumulated Amortization**: Verify the accumulated amortization balance against supporting schedules.\n5. **Review of Supporting Documentation**: Indicate whether you have reviewed relevant documentation.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring Impairment Testing**: Forgetting to document impairment testing can lead to understatements of asset values.\n2. **Incorrect Amortization Method**: Using an incorrect amortization method can result in inaccurate financial reporting.\n3. **Overlooking Documentation Review**: Not reviewing supporting documents can miss critical inconsistencies or errors.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is foundational and feeds into other forms related to the detailed review of intangible assets, such as Form 10.3 (Detailed Intangible Assets) and Form 10.4 (Goodwill). It also depends on",
