    "expertNote": "# Form 110.1: Inventories - Raw materials\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: inventory | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 110.1: Inventories - Raw Materials\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 110.1 is used to document the initial assessment and planning related to raw materials inventories during the onboarding phase of an audit. It helps auditors understand the client's inventory management system and identify key risks.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form at the very beginning of the audit, typically during the onboarding phase, before diving into detailed testing. This ensures you have a solid understanding of how raw materials are managed and stored.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Inventory Management System**: Describe the system used for managing raw materials.\n2. **Storage Locations**: List all locations where raw materials are stored.\n3. **Control Procedures**: Outline key control procedures in place to ensure inventory accuracy.\n4. **Risk Assessment**: Identify potential risks related to raw material inventories.\n5. **Initial Impressions**: Record your initial impressions and observations about the inventory management process.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring Storage Locations**: Forgetting to list all storage locations can lead to incomplete risk assessments.\n2. **Overlooking Control Procedures**: Not documenting control procedures means you might miss important internal controls that mitigate risks.\n3. **Neglecting Risk Assessment**: Skipping this step can result in overlooking significant audit risks.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is foundational and feeds into other inventory-related forms, such as physical count plans (Form 120) and detailed testing schedules (Form 150). It provides the necessary context for subsequent inventory procedures.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form aligns with ISAs related to understanding the entity and its environmen",
