    "expertNote": "# Form 110.3: Inventories - Finished goods\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: inventory | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 110.3 - Inventories - Finished Goods\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 110.3 is used to document the initial assessment of finished goods inventory during the onboarding phase of an audit. It helps auditors understand the client's inventory processes and identify key areas for further testing.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed early in the audit process, typically after the initial risk assessment but before detailed substantive tests. It is used when you need to gather preliminary information about finished goods inventory management and controls.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Inventory Description**: Clearly describe the types of finished goods held by the client.\n2. **Storage Locations**: List where these items are stored, including any third-party locations.\n3. **Control Environment**: Note key internal controls related to inventory management (e.g., physical security, access controls).\n4. **Valuation Method**: Specify how the company values its finished goods inventory.\n5. **Obsolescence Risk**: Assess whether there is a risk of obsolescence or spoilage affecting inventory valuation.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incomplete Descriptions**: Trainees often skip detailed descriptions of inventory items, leading to misunderstandings later in the audit.\n2. **Overlooking Storage Locations**: Not documenting all storage locations can result in missed inventory counts and potential misstatements.\n3. **Ignoring Control Environment**: Failing to assess internal controls can lead to significant risks that are not addressed in subsequent testing.\n\n#### Connections:\nForm 110.3 feeds into other forms like the Inventory Count Plan (Form ID: 120) by providing necessary details about inventory types and storage locations, which are crucial for planning the count procedures. It also depends ",
