    "expertNote": "# Form 110.5: Inventories - Production supplies\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: inventory | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 110.5: Inventories - Production Supplies\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 110.5 is used to document the initial assessment and planning steps for auditing production supplies inventory. It helps ensure that the auditor understands the nature, value, and risks associated with these supplies.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the onboarding phase of an audit, typically early in the engagement when the auditor first assesses the client's inventory management system and processes.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Description of Production Supplies**: Clearly outline what types of production supplies are included.\n2. **Estimated Value**: Provide an estimate of the total value of these supplies to gauge materiality.\n3. **Risk Assessment**: Identify key risks related to the accuracy and completeness of inventory records.\n4. **Internal Controls**: Document internal controls over production supplies, such as receiving procedures or periodic counts.\n5. **Prior Year Adjustments**: Note any adjustments made in previous years for misstatements found.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Overlooking Internal Controls**: Trainees sometimes skip detailing internal controls, which can lead to an incomplete risk assessment.\n2. **Inaccurate Value Estimates**: Underestimating or overestimating the value of production supplies can affect materiality assessments and audit planning.\n3. **Ignoring Prior Year Adjustments**: Not considering past adjustments can result in a failure to recognize recurring issues.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into other inventory-related forms, such as physical count schedules (Form 110.6) and detailed testing procedures (Form 110.7). It also depends on the initial risk assessment (Form 300) completed during the planning phase.\n\n#### ISA Con",
