    "expertNote": "# Form 110: Inventories leadsheet\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: inventory | **Type**: leadsheet\n**ISA**: ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 3 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 110 - Inventories Leadsheet\n\n#### Purpose:\nThe Inventories Leadsheet is a foundational document used to gather initial information about the client's inventory management system. It helps auditors understand the scope and complexity of inventory-related risks early in the audit process.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the onboarding phase, typically at the beginning of the audit engagement or as soon as you have access to basic information about the client’s inventory operations. This allows you to plan your audit strategy effectively.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Inventory Description**: Briefly describe the types and quantities of inventory held by the client.\n2. **Location of Inventory**: List where the inventory is stored, including any third-party locations.\n3. **Inventory Valuation Method**: Specify how the company values its inventory (e.g., FIFO, LIFO).\n4. **Internal Controls**: Note key internal controls over inventory management and handling.\n5. **Significant Transactions**: Highlight any significant inventory transactions during the period.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Omitting Details**: Trainees often skip filling in critical fields due to time pressure or unfamiliarity with the client's operations.\n2. **Inaccurate Valuation Method**: Misidentifying or misunderstanding the company’s inventory valuation method can lead to incorrect audit conclusions.\n3. **Ignoring Third-Party Locations**: Forgetting to include third-party storage locations can result in an incomplete assessment of inventory risks.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form provides essential information that influences other audit forms and procedures, such as the Inventory Detail Test (Form ID: 120) and Physical Inventory Observation (Form ID: 130). It also helps in planning risk assessments a",
