    "expertNote": "# Form 120.120: Other financial assets, current - Substantive analytical procedures\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 120.120: Other Financial Assets, Current - Substantive Analytical Procedures\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 120.120 is used to perform substantive analytical procedures on current other financial assets during the audit process. This helps auditors detect unexpected relationships or fluctuations that may indicate material misstatements.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the planning and review stages of the audit, typically after initial risk assessment but before detailed testing. It’s particularly useful when there are significant changes in the client's financial position or industry trends affecting other financial assets.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Description of Analytical Procedure**: Clearly describe what analytical procedure you will perform (e.g., trend analysis, ratio comparison).\n2. **Expected Results**: Outline what results you expect from your analysis.\n3. **Actual Results**: Record the actual findings from your analysis.\n4. **Evaluation and Conclusion**: Assess whether there are any discrepancies between expected and actual results and draw conclusions.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring Industry Trends**: Failing to consider industry trends or economic conditions can lead to inaccurate expectations.\n2. **Lack of Documentation**: Not documenting the rationale behind the analytical procedures or the evaluation process thoroughly.\n3. **Overlooking Unusual Fluctuations**: Missing unusual fluctuations in financial data that could indicate potential issues.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into the risk assessment and detailed testing phases. The insights gained here can influence the scope and nature of further audit procedures, ensuring a more focused and effective audit.\n\n#### ISA Cont",
