    "expertNote": "# Form 135.120: Prepayments - Substantive analytical procedures\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 1 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 135.120: Prepayments - Substantive Analytical Procedures\n\n**Purpose**:  \nThis form helps auditors assess the reasonableness of prepayment balances by performing substantive analytical procedures during the onboarding phase, ensuring that the financial statements are free from material misstatements.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nComplete this form early in the audit process, typically after initial data collection and before detailed testing. It’s used when there is a need to understand and validate the reasonableness of prepayment balances based on historical trends or industry benchmarks.\n\n**Key Fields**:\n1. **Expected Prepayments Balance**: Enter the expected balance calculated using analytical procedures.\n2. **Actual Prepayments Balance**: Record the actual balance from the financial statements.\n3. **Variance Explanation**: Provide a detailed explanation for any significant variances between expected and actual balances.\n4. **Supporting Documentation**: Attach or reference supporting documents used to calculate the expected balance.\n5. **Conclusion**: Summarize your findings and conclusions regarding the reasonableness of prepayments.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:\n1. **Ignoring Historical Trends**: Forgetting to consider historical trends when calculating expected balances can lead to inaccurate expectations.\n2. **Lack of Documentation**: Not providing sufficient documentation or explanations for variances can result in incomplete audit evidence.\n3. **Overlooking Industry Benchmarks**: Failing to use industry benchmarks as a reference point can miss potential red flags.\n\n**Connections**:\n- **Incoming References**: This form relies on initial data collection and understanding the client’s business operations (Form ID 100.x).\n- **Outgoing Refer",
