    "expertNote": "# Form 1600.3: Staff costs\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: payroll | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 1600.3: Staff Costs\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 1600.3 is used to document the initial review of staff costs during the onboarding phase of an audit. It helps ensure that payroll records are accurate and complete, setting a foundation for further audit procedures.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed early in the audit process, typically after the initial client meeting but before diving into detailed testing of payroll transactions. It’s used when you need to understand the payroll system and verify basic accuracy.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Payroll System Description**: Briefly describe how the payroll system operates.\n2. **Staff Headcount Verification**: Confirm the number of employees on payroll matches HR records.\n3. **Salary Review**: Verify that salary amounts are reasonable and consistent with job descriptions.\n4. **Cost Allocation Method**: Document how costs are allocated across different departments or projects.\n5. **Payroll Processing Schedule**: Note when payrolls are processed to understand timing.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring System Documentation**: Failing to document the payroll system can lead to misunderstandings later in the audit.\n2. **Overlooking Headcount Verification**: Not verifying headcounts against HR records can miss discrepancies early on.\n3. **Neglecting Cost Allocation Details**: Missing cost allocation information can complicate financial reporting accuracy.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into other forms like 1600.4 (Payroll Detail Review) and 1600.5 (Payroll Controls). It provides foundational data that these subsequent forms build upon for more detailed testing.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm 1600.3 satisfies requirements under ISA 330 (Auditor’s Responsibilities Relating to Fraud in an Audit of a Financial Report) by ensuring payroll accu",
