    "expertNote": "# Form 1700.2: Other operating income, area by function\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: revenue | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 1700.2: Other Operating Income, Area by Function\n\n**Purpose**:  \nThis worksheet helps auditors understand the sources of other operating income for each functional area of a business. It aids in identifying and evaluating the completeness and accuracy of this revenue component.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nYou should complete this form during the onboarding phase when you're first getting familiar with the client's operations. This is crucial before diving deeper into audit procedures related to revenue recognition.\n\n**Key Fields**:  \n1. **Function Area**: Clearly define each functional area of the business (e.g., sales, marketing).\n2. **Source of Income**: List all sources of other operating income for each function.\n3. **Amount**: Enter the total amount recognized as other operating income from each source.\n4. **Supporting Documentation**: Specify the documents that support these amounts.\n5. **Evaluation Notes**: Record any observations or issues noted during your initial review.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:  \n1. **Omitting Sources**: Forgetting to list all sources of other operating income can lead to incomplete data.\n2. **Incorrect Amounts**: Entering incorrect figures due to transcription errors or misunderstanding the source documentation.\n3. **Lack of Documentation**: Not specifying supporting documents, which is crucial for traceability and verification.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form provides foundational information that feeds into more detailed audit procedures in later phases. It helps identify areas requiring further investigation, such as revenue cut-off testing or substantiation of income sources.\n\n**ISA Context**:  \nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form supports the general requirements for understanding and documenting other operating income under",
