    "expertNote": "# Form 2.105: Issues - My issues\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 2.105: Issues - My issues\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 2.105 is used to document any issues encountered during the audit process that are specific to your responsibilities or observations. It helps in tracking and addressing these issues systematically.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nYou should complete this form whenever you identify an issue during the testing phase of the audit, such as discrepancies in financial statements, unusual transactions, or other matters that require attention.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Issue Description**: Clearly describe what the issue is.\n2. **Date Identified**: Record when you first noticed the issue.\n3. **Implications**: Explain the potential impact of the issue on the audit and financial statements.\n4. **Actions Taken**: Detail any steps you have already taken to address the issue.\n5. **Follow-up Required**: Indicate if further investigation or action is needed.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Lack of Clarity**: Failing to provide a detailed description can make it difficult for others to understand and act on the issue.\n2. **Ignoring Implications**: Not considering the broader impact of an issue can lead to overlooking significant problems.\n3. **Omitting Actions Taken**: Forgetting to document what you've already done can result in duplicate work or missed opportunities to resolve issues promptly.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is typically used alongside other forms that track audit findings and issues, such as Form 2.104 (Issues - Audit Team). It feeds into the overall risk assessment and helps shape the audit strategy by identifying areas that need more attention.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile this form does not directly reference specific ISAs, it supports several auditing principles, including those related to planning and supervision of an audit (ISA 220), risk asses",
