    "expertNote": "# Form 2.25: Trial balance - By leadsheet\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: leadsheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 2.25: Trial Balance - By Leadsheet\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 2.25 is used to review and analyze the trial balance, ensuring that all account balances are accurate and properly classified before further testing.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the testing phase of the audit, typically after the preliminary review of financial statements but before detailed substantive tests. It’s crucial when you need to verify the accuracy and completeness of the trial balance entries.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Account Number**: Ensure this is correctly listed as per the general ledger.\n2. **Description**: Verify that the account description matches the chart of accounts.\n3. **Balance**: Double-check for any discrepancies between the trial balance and the source documents.\n4. **Adjustments Needed**: Identify if any adjustments are necessary to correct errors or omissions.\n5. **Review Comments**: Document your findings and any issues identified during the review.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect Account Balances**: Forgetting to update balances after corrections or adjustments.\n2. **Omitting Adjustments**: Failing to note required adjustments can lead to inaccurate financial statements.\n3. **Ignoring Review Comments**: Not documenting discrepancies or issues can result in missed audit opportunities.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is a foundational step that feeds into other testing forms, such as the Substantive Tests of Details (Form 2.40) and Analytical Procedures (Form 2.50). It relies on accurate data from the general ledger and source documents.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm 2.25 aligns with **ISA 330 – Audit Evidence** by ensuring that audit evidence is sufficient, appropriate, and relevant to support the financial statements. It also ties into **ISA 500 – General Req",
