    "expertNote": "# Form 2.30: Trial balance - By map no\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 1 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 2.30: Trial Balance - By Map No.\n\n#### Purpose:\nThe Trial Balance by Map Number form helps auditors verify the accuracy of the trial balance entries by mapping them to specific accounts or schedules. This ensures that all financial statements are correctly supported and accurately represented.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nYou should complete this form during the testing phase, typically after you have reviewed the preliminary trial balance and identified the relevant account mappings. It’s crucial when there are discrepancies or when detailed verification of account balances is necessary.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Account Number**: Ensure you correctly input the account numbers from the trial balance.\n2. **Map No.**: This field links the trial balance entries to specific audit schedules or working papers.\n3. **Debit/Credit Amounts**: Verify that these amounts match those in the trial balance and are accurately recorded.\n4. **Description**: Provide a brief description of each account for clarity.\n5. **Comments/Adjustments**: Note any discrepancies, adjustments needed, or comments about the entries.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect Mapping**: Trainees often map accounts incorrectly to audit schedules, leading to errors in subsequent testing.\n2. **Omission of Entries**: Forgetting to include certain trial balance items can result in incomplete audit coverage.\n3. **Inaccurate Amounts**: Entering incorrect debit or credit amounts can skew the entire trial balance verification process.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is a critical step before detailed account analysis and reconciliations. It feeds into other forms like the Detailed Account Analysis (Form 2.40) and Reconciliation of Accounts (Form 3.10), ensuring that all entries are correctly mapped and verified.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nThis ",
