    "expertNote": "# Form 2.35: Trial balance - By account number\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Form ID: 2.35 - Trial Balance by Account Number\n\n#### Purpose:\nThe Trial Balance by Account Number form is used to verify the accuracy of the client's financial records by listing all account balances at a specific date. This helps auditors ensure that all transactions are correctly recorded and supports the preparation of financial statements.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the testing phase of the audit, typically after reviewing the preliminary trial balance and before detailed substantive tests. It is used whenever there's a need to confirm account balances or when discrepancies are identified.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Account Number**: Ensure this matches the client’s chart of accounts.\n2. **Account Description**: Verify that descriptions align with standard accounting practices.\n3. **Debit/Credit Balance**: Double-check these figures for accuracy and consistency.\n4. **Adjustments**: Record any necessary adjustments to correct errors or omissions.\n5. **Total Balance**: Confirm that the sum of all debits equals the sum of all credits.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect Account Numbers**: Entering wrong account numbers can lead to significant errors in financial reporting.\n2. **Omission of Adjustments**: Forgetting to include necessary adjustments can result in inaccurate balances.\n3. **Calculation Errors**: Simple arithmetic mistakes can occur, affecting the overall trial balance.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is crucial for preparing the adjusted trial balance and serves as a basis for further audit procedures such as substantive tests of details. It relies on accurate data from the client’s general ledger and may feed into other forms like the Substantive Tests of Details Worksheet (Form 2.36).\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this fo",
