    "expertNote": "# Form 2.55: Elimination entries\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 2.55 - Elimination Entries\n\n**Purpose**:  \nForm 2.55 is used to document the elimination entries required when consolidating financial statements of a group of companies. This ensures that intercompany transactions and balances are appropriately removed from the consolidated figures.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nThis form should be completed during the testing phase (Audit Phase: 4) after you have identified and gathered all relevant intercompany transactions and balances. It is essential when preparing or reviewing consolidation entries for a group of companies.\n\n**Key Fields**:  \n1. **Description of Elimination Entry**: Clearly describe what each elimination entry represents, such as eliminating sales to subsidiaries.\n2. **Debit Account**: Specify the account being debited in the elimination entry.\n3. **Credit Account**: Specify the account being credited in the elimination entry.\n4. **Amount**: Enter the monetary amount for each elimination entry.\n5. **Reference Document**: Include any supporting documents or references that justify the elimination entries.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:  \n1. **Incorrect Amounts**: Trainees often enter incorrect amounts due to calculation errors or misreading of intercompany transactions.\n2. **Omitting Entries**: Forgetting to include all necessary elimination entries, especially those involving complex transactions.\n3. **Improper Account Selection**: Choosing the wrong accounts for debits and credits, leading to inaccurate consolidation figures.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form feeds into the Consolidated Financial Statements worksheet (Form ID 2.60) where you will input the final consolidated figures after all eliminations have been made. It also depends on the Intercompany Transactions worksheet (Form ID 2.54) for identifying and documenting intercompany transact",
