    "expertNote": "# Form 300.2: Non-interest-bearing borrowings, non-current\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: expenditure | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 300.2: Non-interest-bearing borrowings, non-current\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 300.2 is used to document the audit procedures related to non-interest-bearing borrowings that are classified as non-current assets. This form helps ensure that these borrowings are properly recorded and disclosed in the financial statements.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nYou should complete this form during the testing phase of your audit, specifically when you are reviewing long-term liabilities or non-current assets. It is particularly relevant if the entity has significant non-interest-bearing borrowings that need to be verified.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Description of Borrowing**: Clearly describe the nature and terms of each borrowing.\n2. **Amount**: Enter the total amount of the borrowing, ensuring accuracy.\n3. **Maturity Date**: Specify when the borrowing is due for repayment.\n4. **Collateral (if any)**: Note if there is any collateral securing the borrowing.\n5. **Audit Evidence Obtained**: Document the evidence you gathered to support your findings.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect Amounts**: Entering incorrect amounts can lead to material misstatements in the financial statements.\n2. **Omitting Collateral Details**: Forgetting to record collateral details can result in an incomplete audit trail.\n3. **Lack of Supporting Evidence**: Not documenting the evidence you used can weaken your audit support.\n\n#### Connections:\nForm 300.2 is typically connected with other forms related to long-term liabilities and non-current assets, such as Form 300 (Long-Term Liabilities) or Form 410 (Property, Plant, and Equipment). It ensures that all aspects of the borrowings are properly addressed in the audit.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form aligns wit",
