    "expertNote": "# Form 330: Other liabilities, non-current leadsheet\n\n**Phase**: 3_risk | **Category**: general | **Type**: leadsheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 4 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID 330: Other Liabilities, Non-Current Leadsheet\n\n**Purpose**: This leadsheet helps auditors summarize and analyze non-current other liabilities, ensuring they are accurately recorded and properly disclosed.\n\n**When to Complete**: You should complete this form during the risk assessment phase of your audit. It's crucial when you identify significant non-current liabilities that need detailed examination.\n\n**Key Fields**:\n1. **Liability Description**: Clearly describe each liability.\n2. **Amount**: Enter the current book value of each liability.\n3. **Maturity Date**: Specify when the liability is due for payment.\n4. **Accrual Basis**: Indicate whether the liability is recognized on an accrual basis.\n5. **Disclosure Note**: Mention any relevant notes or disclosures in the financial statements.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:\n1. **Inaccurate Descriptions**: Failing to provide clear, detailed descriptions can lead to misunderstandings about the nature of the liabilities.\n2. **Omission of Maturity Dates**: Not entering maturity dates can result in misinterpretation of when payments are due.\n3. **Neglecting Disclosure Notes**: Forgetting to reference relevant disclosures can cause issues with compliance and transparency.\n\n**Connections**: This form feeds into the risk assessment process, influencing the design of further audit procedures. It also depends on information gathered from other forms that detail specific liabilities.\n\n**ISA Context**: While no specific ISA references are listed, this form supports several auditing standards by ensuring accurate identification, measurement, and disclosure of non-current liabilities, aligning with ISAs related to risk assessment and financial statement disclosures.\n",
    "isaStandards": [
      {
        "standard": "ISA 260",
        "title": "Communication with Those Charged with Governance",
        "scope": "Audit scope, significant findings, independence",
        "when_used": "Phase 2 Planning and Phase 5 Completion"
      }
    ],
