    "expertNote": "# Form 335: Misstatements Summary\n\n**Phase**: 3_risk | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 6 in, 6 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 335 - Misstatements Summary\n\n**Purpose**\nThe Misstatements Summary form helps auditors document and aggregate misstatements identified during the audit process to assess their materiality and overall impact on the financial statements.\n\n**When to Complete**\nThis form is completed during the risk assessment phase, typically after identifying misstatements in various accounts or transactions. It's used to compile all documented misstatements for a comprehensive review of their significance.\n\n**Key Fields**\n1. **Misstatement Description**: Clearly describe each identified misstatement.\n2. **Amount**: Enter the financial amount of each misstatement.\n3. **Materiality Level**: Indicate whether the misstatement is material or immaterial.\n4. **Correction Required**: Specify if a correction is needed and what actions will be taken.\n\n**Common Mistakes**\n1. **Incomplete Descriptions**: Failing to provide detailed descriptions can lead to misunderstandings about the nature of the misstatements.\n2. **Omission of Materiality Assessment**: Not assessing materiality for each misstatement can result in overlooking significant issues.\n3. **Lack of Action Plan**: Forgetting to outline necessary corrections or follow-up actions can delay resolution.\n\n**Connections**\nThis form feeds into the Audit Summary and Review (Form ID 905) by providing a consolidated list of misstatements that need further evaluation. It also depends on other forms like the Preliminary Engagement Activities (Form ID 100) for initial risk assessments.\n\n**ISA Context**\nThe Misstatements Summary form satisfies requirements under ISA 330 (The Auditor’s Responsibilities Relating to Materiality in an Audit of a Financial Statement) and ISA 500 (Audit Evidence). It ensures that auditors properly identify, document, and evaluate misst",
    "isaStandards": [
      {
        "standard": "ISA 240",
        "title": "The Auditor's Responsibilities Relating to Fraud",
        "scope": "Fraud risk factors, management override, journal entry testing",
        "when_used": "Phase 3 Risk Assessment — fraud risk is always presumed significant"
      }
    ],
    "fieldDependencies": []
