    "expertNote": "# Form 335.14: Adjusted journal entries - corrected by client\n\n**Phase**: 3_risk | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 1 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 335.14: Adjusted Journal Entries - Corrected by Client\n\n**Purpose**:  \nForm 335.14 is used to document journal entries that the client has corrected during the audit process. This form helps ensure that all adjustments are properly reviewed and recorded, maintaining the accuracy of the financial statements.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nYou should complete this form when the client makes corrections to previously reviewed journal entries. It's typically done in the risk assessment phase (Audit Phase 3) but can be used throughout the audit process as needed.\n\n**Key Fields**:  \n1. **Entry Date**: The date of the corrected journal entry.\n2. **Description**: A clear description of what the adjustment is correcting.\n3. **Account Details**: Include account numbers and descriptions for both debits and credits.\n4. **Amounts**: Enter the amounts involved in the correction, ensuring they match the client’s records.\n5. **Client Reviewer**: Indicate who reviewed the corrected entries on behalf of the client.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:  \n1. **Incorrect Amounts**: Trainees often enter incorrect or inconsistent amounts, leading to errors in financial statements.\n2. **Incomplete Descriptions**: Providing vague descriptions can obscure the purpose of the adjustment, making it harder to verify later.\n3. **Failing to Update References**: Not updating references to other forms or documents that may be affected by these corrections.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form is often used alongside Form 335.10 (Adjusted Journal Entries - Identified by Auditor) and depends on the initial review of journal entries. It ensures that all adjustments, whether identified by the auditor or corrected by the client, are documented accurately.\n\n**ISA Context**:  \nForm 335.14 supports ISA 330 (Auditor’s Respons",
