    "expertNote": "# Form 335.15: Adjusted journal entries from client\n\n**Phase**: 3_risk | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 1 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 335.15: Adjusted Journal Entries from Client\n\n**Purpose**:  \nForm 335.15 is used to document adjusted journal entries provided by the client. It helps auditors ensure that all necessary adjustments are considered and properly evaluated during the audit process.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nYou should complete this form after you have reviewed the client’s proposed adjusting entries, typically during the risk assessment phase of the audit. This ensures that any material adjustments are identified early in the audit process.\n\n**Key Fields**:\n1. **Entry Description**: Clearly describe what each journal entry is for.\n2. **Debit/Credit Accounts**: Ensure accurate listing of accounts being debited and credited.\n3. **Amount**: Verify the accuracy of the amounts involved in each entry.\n4. **Supporting Documentation**: Note any documentation or evidence supporting the entries.\n5. **Review Comments**: Include your review comments or questions regarding the entries.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:\n1. **Omitting Details**: Forgetting to provide sufficient detail about the nature and purpose of each journal entry can lead to misunderstandings.\n2. **Incorrect Amounts**: Entering incorrect amounts can result in misstatements that affect financial statements.\n3. **Lack of Documentation**: Failing to reference supporting documentation can weaken the audit trail.\n\n**Connections**:\n- This form is typically completed after reviewing the client’s trial balance and before performing detailed substantive tests on specific accounts (e.g., Form 340 for revenue).\n- It feeds into other forms like the Management Representation Letter (Form 510) where you might need to confirm certain adjustments.\n\n**ISA Context**:\n- **ISA 330**: This form supports the auditor’s responsibility to understand an",
