    "expertNote": "# Form 35: Receivables, non-current leadsheet\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: revenue | **Type**: leadsheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 35 - Receivables, Non-Current Leadsheet\n\n#### Purpose:\nThis form is used to summarize and analyze non-current receivables, helping auditors assess the accuracy and completeness of these accounts in the financial statements.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form during the testing phase of the audit when you are reviewing long-term receivables. This typically follows the initial assessment and planning stages.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Account Number**: Ensure you accurately input the account number for each non-current receivable.\n2. **Description**: Provide a clear description of what the receivable relates to, such as a loan or lease payment.\n3. **Balance**: Enter the current balance of the receivable as per the client’s records.\n4. **Age Analysis**: Fill in the age analysis fields to categorize how long these receivables have been outstanding (e.g., 1-2 years, over 5 years).\n5. **Impairment Assessment**: Document any impairment assessments or provisions made for uncollectible amounts.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect Account Numbers**: Entering the wrong account number can lead to inaccurate analysis and reporting.\n2. **Neglecting Age Analysis**: Failing to complete age analysis can miss critical insights into the risk of non-payment.\n3. **Overlooking Impairment Assessment**: Not documenting impairment assessments can result in underestimating bad debt risks.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into the overall assessment of receivables and is often referenced by other forms, such as the aging schedule (Form ID: 10) or the impairment analysis (Form ID: 25). It provides detailed information that supports conclusions drawn on these related forms.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form aligns with ISAs related to revenue recognition (ISA",
    "isaStandards": [],
