    "expertNote": "# Form 360-3: Key Audit Matters (KAM)\n\n**Phase**: 5_completion | **Category**: it_controls | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 315, ISA 705 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 360-3: Key Audit Matters (KAM)\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 360-3 is used to document the key audit matters identified during an audit. This form helps ensure that the auditor communicates effectively with stakeholders about the most significant issues addressed in the audit.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form is completed during the completion phase of the audit, typically after all substantive testing and other audit procedures are finished but before issuing the final audit report. It should be filled out when there are specific matters that were complex or uncertain and required significant auditor judgment.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Key Audit Matter Description**: Clearly describe the matter.\n2. **How the Matter Relates to Financial Statements**: Explain its impact on the financial statements.\n3. **Auditor’s Response**: Detail how you addressed this matter during the audit.\n4. **Conclusion**: Summarize your findings and conclusions regarding the matter.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Lack of Clarity**: Trainees often write vague descriptions that do not clearly convey the significance of the key audit matters.\n2. **Omission of Responses**: Forgetting to document how specific audit procedures were applied to address the matter.\n3. **Insufficient Detail**: Not providing enough detail in the conclusion, leading to unclear communication.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is closely linked with other forms that document significant audit findings and judgments, such as Form 350-1 (Auditor’s Responses to Management Representation Letter) and Form 420-1 (Management Letters). It ensures that all critical issues are properly addressed and communicated in the final report.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm 360-3 satisfies requirements under ISA 315 (Communication with Those Charged with Gov",
