    "expertNote": "# Form 367: Audit findings - Sample letter\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: it_controls | **Type**: letter\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form ID 367: Audit Findings - Sample Letter\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm ID 367 is used to draft a letter summarizing audit findings related to IT controls during the onboarding phase. This helps in clearly communicating issues and recommendations to stakeholders.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form after conducting IT control audits and identifying any significant findings or discrepancies that need to be communicated to management or relevant parties.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Recipient**: Ensure you specify the correct recipient of the letter.\n2. **Date**: Enter the date when the letter is being drafted.\n3. **Summary of Findings**: Clearly outline the key IT control issues identified during the audit.\n4. **Recommendations**: Provide actionable recommendations to address the findings.\n5. **Sign-off**: Include necessary signatures or approvals.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Omitting Key Details**: Forgetting to include critical information about the findings can lead to misunderstandings.\n2. **Lack of Clarity**: Writing vague or unclear recommendations can make it difficult for management to take corrective actions.\n3. **Neglecting Sign-offs**: Not getting proper approvals before sending the letter can undermine its authority and effectiveness.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is typically used after completing various IT control audit procedures (Procedures: 15) and may reference other forms that document specific findings or test results. It serves as a summary and communication tool, feeding into management reports and potentially influencing future audit plans.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm ID 367 aligns with **ISA 330 - Communication with Those Charged with Governance** by ensuring clear and timely communication of significant audit findings. It also supports **ISA 500",
