    "expertNote": "# Form 4.40: History - Document modification\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 1 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 4.40: History - Document Modification\n\n**Purpose**:  \nForm 4.40 helps track changes made to documents during the audit process. This ensures transparency and accountability for any modifications, which is crucial for maintaining audit integrity.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nYou should complete this form whenever you make a modification to an important document during your testing phase. It’s particularly useful when changes are significant or when there's a need to document why a change was made.\n\n**Key Fields**:\n1. **Document Name**: Clearly state the name of the document that was modified.\n2. **Date of Modification**: Record the exact date and time when the modification occurred.\n3. **Description of Changes**: Provide a detailed description of what changes were made.\n4. **Reason for Change**: Explain why the change was necessary.\n5. **Person Making the Change**: Identify who made the modification.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:\n1. **Omitting Details**: Trainees often skip filling in all required fields, especially the \"Reason for Change,\" which is crucial for understanding the context of modifications.\n2. **Inconsistent Formatting**: Not maintaining a consistent format can make it difficult to track changes over time.\n3. **Failing to Sign Off**: Forgetting to sign or initial the form after making entries can lead to confusion about who made specific changes.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form is typically referenced by other audit forms that require documentation of document history, such as Form 4.10 (Document Review). It ensures that all modifications are accounted for and traceable throughout the audit process.\n\n**ISA Context**:  \nWhile this form doesn't directly reference any specific ISA requirement, it supports several auditing principles outlined in ISAs, including maintaining",
