    "expertNote": "# Form 400-2: Optimiser checklist - Profile 5\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: checklist\n**ISA**: ISA 220 (Revised), ISA 600 (Revised) | **Connections**: 0 in, 4 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 400-2 - Optimiser Checklist - Profile 5\n\n#### Purpose:\nThe Optimiser checklist (Profile 5) is used to ensure that all necessary steps are taken during the onboarding phase of an audit engagement. It helps auditors systematically review and document the initial setup of the audit, ensuring compliance with standards and best practices.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed at the very beginning of the audit engagement, typically after accepting the client but before commencing detailed audit procedures. It is crucial for setting up the audit framework correctly.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Client Information**: Ensure all details about the client are accurate and complete.\n2. **Audit Objectives**: Clearly define what you aim to achieve with this audit.\n3. **Risk Assessment**: Identify key risks associated with the audit engagement.\n4. **Engagement Team Members**: List all team members involved in the audit, including their roles.\n5. **Compliance Requirements**: Document any specific compliance requirements that need to be addressed.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incomplete Client Information**: Forgetting to fill out critical details about the client can lead to misunderstandings later.\n2. **Overlooking Risk Assessment**: Not thoroughly identifying risks can result in missing important audit areas.\n3. **Neglecting Team Member Roles**: Failing to specify roles and responsibilities can cause confusion and inefficiency.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into other forms by establishing a solid foundation for the audit engagement. For example, it provides essential information that is used in subsequent risk assessments (Form 401) and audit planning documents (Form 300).\n\n#### ISA Context:\nThe Optimiser checklist satisfies requirements un",
