            "description": "Where possible, review the previous auditor's or accountant's working papers and make notes of relevant information, such as: ∙ Composition of opening balances, including disclosures ∙ Application of accounting policies ∙ Uncorrected misstatements ∙ Significant audit findings ∙ Business and fraud risk factors ∙ The control environment ∙ Key control activities ∙ Impact of general IT controls ∙ Preparation of estimates ∙ Related-party transactions ∙ Going-concern events/conditions ∙ Difficulties encountered in the audit ∙ Disagreements with management ∙ Evidence of management bias ∙ Need for special audit procedures ∙ Need for consultation or use of experts",
