    "expertNote": "# Form 425.110: Accounts payable confirmation - Supplementary procedures\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: expenditure | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 505, ISA 530 | **Connections**: 2 in, 5 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 425.110: Accounts payable confirmation - Supplementary procedures\n\n**Purpose:**  \nThis form is used to document supplementary audit procedures when accounts payable confirmations are incomplete or inconclusive. It helps ensure that the auditor has sufficient evidence regarding the completeness and accuracy of accounts payable balances.\n\n**When to Complete:**  \nYou should complete this form during the testing phase of your audit, specifically after you have sent out accounts payable confirmations and received responses that are either incomplete or raise questions about the data's integrity.\n\n**Key Fields:**\n1. **Description of Inconclusive Items**: Clearly describe which items from the confirmation process were inconclusive.\n2. **Supplementary Procedures Performed**: Detail what additional procedures (like alternative testing) you conducted to verify these items.\n3. **Evaluation of Results**: Summarize how the results of your supplementary procedures affect your audit opinion and conclusions.\n4. **Conclusion**: State whether the supplementary procedures provided sufficient evidence to support the recorded balances.\n5. **Documentation of Evidence**: Attach or reference any supporting documentation from your supplementary testing.\n\n**Common Mistakes:**\n1. **Failing to Document Adequately:** Trainees often skip detailed descriptions, leading to insufficient audit trail and potential gaps in evidence.\n2. **Not Following Up on Inconclusive Results:** Not performing adequate follow-up procedures can result in incomplete or inaccurate audit conclusions.\n3. **Ignoring ISA Requirements:** Not adhering strictly to the requirements of ISA 505 (Audit Evidence) and ISA 530 (Substantive Analytical Procedures) can lead to non-compliance i",
