    "expertNote": "# Form 425.2: Other payables\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: expenditure | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 425.2: Other Payables\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 425.2 is used to test the accuracy and completeness of other payables listed on the financial statements. This form helps auditors ensure that all liabilities are properly recorded and supported by valid documentation.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form during the testing phase of the audit, typically after you have reviewed the client's internal controls related to payable transactions and identified a sample for detailed examination.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Payable Description**: Clearly describe the nature of each payable.\n2. **Amount**: Enter the exact amount recorded in the financial statements.\n3. **Supporting Documentation**: Specify what type of documentation supports the payable (e.g., invoices, contracts).\n4. **Review Status**: Indicate whether the supporting documents have been reviewed and if they match the recorded amounts.\n5. **Comments/Findings**: Note any discrepancies or issues found during the review.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring Documentation**: Forgetting to request or review supporting documentation for each payable can lead to unverified entries.\n2. **Inconsistent Descriptions**: Using vague or inconsistent descriptions that do not clearly identify the nature of the payable.\n3. **Overlooking Comments**: Not documenting findings or discrepancies, which can result in missed audit adjustments.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is typically used in conjunction with other testing forms related to payables and accounts payable aging schedules. It helps ensure that all data fed into these schedules is accurate and supported by evidence.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed for this form, it aligns with the general requirements of ISAs 230 (Auditor’s Responsibilities Relating to Fraud in a",
