    "expertNote": "# Form 425: Payables leadsheet\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: expenditure | **Type**: leadsheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 1 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID 425: Payables Leadsheet\n\n**Purpose:**  \nThe Payables leadsheet is a crucial document used to summarize key data about payables for audit testing. It helps auditors organize and analyze vendor payments, ensuring that they are accurate and properly recorded.\n\n**When to Complete:**  \nThis form should be completed during the testing phase of the audit, specifically when reviewing and testing accounts payable transactions. Auditors typically fill it out after gathering initial information from client records and before performing detailed substantive tests.\n\n**Key Fields:**\n1. **Vendor Name**: Ensure you capture the correct vendor name to avoid confusion with similar names.\n2. **Invoice Number**: This is critical for tracing payments back to supporting documents.\n3. **Payment Date**: Verify that this matches the payment date in the client’s records.\n4. **Amount Paid**: Double-check the accuracy of amounts paid to vendors.\n5. **Approval Status**: Confirm whether payments were properly authorized.\n\n**Common Mistakes:**\n1. **Incorrect Vendor Names**: Mixing up vendor names can lead to incorrect analysis and testing.\n2. **Omitting Invoice Numbers**: Forgetting to include invoice numbers makes it impossible to trace transactions back to supporting documents.\n3. **Ignoring Approval Status**: Not verifying if payments were authorized can result in overlooking unauthorized or fraudulent transactions.\n\n**Connections:**\nThis form is typically filled out before detailed substantive tests are performed, such as those documented on other forms like the Vouching for Payments form (Form ID 426). It serves as a starting point and summary that feeds into more specific testing procedures.\n\n**ISA Context:**\nWhile no ISA references are explicitly listed, this form aligns with ISAs related to audit evidence gatheri",
