    "expertNote": "# Form 428: Worksheet - Selecting an auditor's expert\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 1 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID 428: Worksheet - Selecting an Auditor's Expert\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 428 helps auditors document the selection process for engaging experts to assist with specific audit tasks. This ensures that the auditor can rely on the expert’s knowledge and objectivity.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form during the testing phase when you need to engage an external or internal expert to provide specialized knowledge, such as in complex financial instruments or valuation matters.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Expert's Name and Contact Information**: Ensure accuracy for clear communication.\n2. **Reason for Engaging Expert**: Clearly state why their expertise is needed.\n3. **Scope of Work**: Define what the expert will do to avoid misunderstandings.\n4. **Independence Assessment**: Document your evaluation of the expert’s independence.\n5. **Agreement Terms**: Summarize key terms agreed upon, including fees and confidentiality.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Not Clearly Defining Scope**: Forgetting to specify exactly what the expert will do can lead to misaligned expectations.\n2. **Ignoring Independence**: Failing to assess or document independence can compromise audit integrity.\n3. **Overlooking Agreement Terms**: Not recording key terms of engagement can cause legal issues later.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is typically completed before engaging an expert and feeds into other forms like the Engagement Letter (Form ID 102) where details about the expert's role might be included. It also supports the Audit Planning Memorandum (Form ID 403) by documenting decisions made during planning.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, this form aligns with ISAs related to engagement of experts, such as ISA 610: Communicating with Governance, Management and Others in the Audit o",
