    "expertNote": "# Form 436-1: Team planning discussions\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: general | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 436-1: Team Planning Discussions\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 436-1 is used to document the key discussions and decisions made during team planning meetings. It ensures that all team members are aligned on the audit strategy, risk assessment, and resource allocation.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed after the initial planning meeting with the audit team. Typically, this happens early in the planning phase of an audit, before detailed procedures are finalized.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Date of Meeting**: The exact date when the team planning discussion took place.\n2. **Attendees**: Names and roles of all participants in the meeting.\n3. **Key Topics Discussed**: Summary of main topics covered during the meeting, such as audit scope, risk assessment, and resource allocation.\n4. **Decisions Made**: Specific decisions reached by the team regarding audit strategy and procedures.\n5. **Action Items**: Tasks assigned to team members following the meeting.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Omitting Attendees**: Forgetting to list all participants can lead to confusion about who was involved in key discussions.\n2. **Lack of Specificity**: Vague summaries of topics and decisions make it difficult for future reference.\n3. **Ignoring Action Items**: Not documenting tasks assigned can result in incomplete follow-up actions.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is foundational for other planning forms, such as the Audit Plan (Form 401) and Risk Assessment (Form 425). It provides critical information that informs these subsequent documents.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile Form 436-1 does not directly reference specific ISAs, it supports several auditing standards by ensuring effective communication and alignment within the audit team. For example, it aligns with ISA 315 (Understanding the Entity and ",
    "isaStandards": [],
    "fieldDependencies": []
