    "expertNote": "# Form 5003: Group audit - Group audit plan\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: group_audit | **Type**: checklist\n**ISA**: ISA 600 | **Connections**: 2 in, 8 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form ID 5003: Group Audit Plan\n\n#### Purpose:\nThe Group Audit - Group Audit Plan form helps auditors outline the strategy and scope for auditing a group entity. It ensures all critical aspects are considered before diving into detailed audit procedures.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form is completed during the planning phase of an audit, typically after initial risk assessment and understanding of the group structure. Auditors use it to set the direction for the entire audit process.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Group Structure**: Clearly defining the parent company and subsidiaries.\n2. **Risk Assessment**: Identifying significant risks at both the group and component levels.\n3. **Materiality Levels**: Setting materiality thresholds for the group and components.\n4. **Audit Approach**: Detailing how each component will be audited (e.g., full scope, agreed-upon procedures).\n5. **Communication Plan**: Outlining how communication with component auditors will occur.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Ignoring Component Risks**: Failing to adequately assess risks at the subsidiary level can lead to insufficient audit coverage.\n2. **Overlooking Materiality Levels**: Incorrectly setting materiality levels can result in inadequate or excessive testing.\n3. **Poor Communication Plan**: Not detailing how communication will occur with component auditors can cause delays and misunderstandings.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is foundational for other planning documents like the Component Audit Engagement Letter (Form ID 5012) and the Group Audit Report (Form ID 5040). It also influences the Group Financial Statements Review Checklist (Form ID 5038).\n\n#### ISA Context:\nThe form satisfies requirements under ISA 600, which covers the overall audit strategy and planning. Specifically, it ensures th",
