    "expertNote": "# Form 5007: Group audit - Preparation of group audit instructions\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: group_audit | **Type**: checklist\n**ISA**: ISA 600 | **Connections**: 2 in, 4 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form ID: 5007 - Group Audit - Preparation of Group Audit Instructions\n\n#### Purpose:\nThis form helps auditors outline the key instructions for conducting a group audit, ensuring all team members understand their roles and responsibilities.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form during the planning phase of an audit. It should be filled out after initial risk assessments are completed and before detailed audit procedures are planned.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Audit Objectives**: Clearly define what you aim to achieve with the group audit.\n2. **Scope of Work**: Specify which entities will be audited and the extent of work required for each.\n3. **Risk Assessment**: Identify significant risks related to the group structure and financial statements.\n4. **Communication Plan**: Outline how communication will occur among team members and stakeholders.\n5. **Resource Allocation**: Detail who will perform specific tasks and when.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Omitting Specific Objectives**: Forgetting to specify clear, measurable objectives can lead to confusion.\n2. **Neglecting Risk Assessment**: Skipping this step can result in overlooking critical risks that could impact the audit.\n3. **Poor Communication Plan**: Not detailing how communication will happen can cause misunderstandings and inefficiencies.\n\n#### Connections:\n- **Incoming References**: This form builds on information from risk assessments (Form ID 2).\n- **Outgoing References**: It provides instructions that are used in detailed planning forms (Form IDs 4).\n\n#### ISA Context:\nThis form satisfies requirements under ISA 600, which outlines the auditor's responsibilities regarding communication with those charged with governance and other reporting parties. Specifically, it ensures that there is a clear und",
