    "expertNote": "# Form 520E.3: Risk Report - Business risk\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: general | **Type**: report\n**ISA**: ISA 330 | **Connections**: 4 in, 4 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 520E.3: Risk Report - Business Risk\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 520E.3 is used to identify and document business risks that could impact the financial statements. This form helps auditors understand the broader context of the client's operations, which in turn guides risk assessment and audit planning.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the planning phase of the audit, typically after initial discussions with management and before designing detailed audit procedures. It is crucial when there are significant changes in the business environment or new risks identified.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Risk Description**: Clearly define what the risk is.\n2. **Impact on Financial Statements**: Explain how this risk could affect the financial statements.\n3. **Likelihood of Occurrence**: Assess the probability of the risk occurring.\n4. **Management Response**: Document any actions management has taken or plans to take regarding the risk.\n5. **Audit Response**: Outline what audit procedures will be performed to address the risk.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Overlooking Risks**: Trainees may miss identifying significant business risks, leading to inadequate audit planning.\n2. **Inadequate Documentation**: Not providing enough detail in fields like \"Impact on Financial Statements\" can result in unclear audit trails.\n3. **Ignoring Management Response**: Failing to document management’s actions or plans can weaken the overall risk assessment.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into other planning documents, such as the Audit Plan (Form 520E.1) and the Risk Assessment Report (Form 520E.4). It also depends on information gathered from client interviews and preliminary reviews of financial statements.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm 520E.3 aligns with **ISA 330 – The Auditor’s Respo",
