    "expertNote": "# Form 520E.5: Risk Report - Summary of control risk assessment\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: general | **Type**: report\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 1 in, 11 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form 520E.5: Risk Report - Summary of Control Risk Assessment\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 520E.5 is used to summarize the auditor's assessment of control risks for a given audit. This form helps in identifying and documenting the level of risk associated with internal controls, which is crucial for planning the scope of the audit.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the planning phase of the audit, typically after initial risk assessments have been performed and before detailed audit procedures are planned. It's essential when there are significant risks that need to be addressed in the audit plan.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Control Risk Assessment**: This field requires you to rate the level of control risk (high, medium, low) for each identified risk area.\n2. **Description of Control**: Briefly describe the controls in place and their effectiveness.\n3. **Risk Factors**: List any factors that contribute to the assessed risk level.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Inadequate Risk Assessment**: Trainees often underestimate or overestimate control risks, leading to an incorrect audit plan.\n2. **Lack of Specificity**: Not providing enough detail in the description of controls can result in misunderstandings about their effectiveness.\n3. **Ignoring Changes**: Failing to update risk assessments when there are changes in internal controls during the audit period.\n\n#### Connections:\n- **Incoming References**: This form is typically populated with information from earlier risk assessment forms (e.g., Form 520E.1).\n- **Outgoing References**: The summarized control risks feed into the detailed audit plan and other subsequent audit procedures, ensuring that the audit scope addresses all significant risks.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nThis form aligns with ISA 330, which",
