    "expertNote": "# Form 520E.6: Risk Report - Risk assessment\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: general | **Type**: report\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form 520E.6: Risk Report - Risk Assessment\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm 520E.6 is used to document the auditor's assessment of risks associated with the financial statements during the planning phase. It helps in identifying and evaluating significant risks, which are crucial for designing effective audit procedures.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed early in the audit process, typically after initial discussions with management and before detailed planning. It is essential when you need to assess the risk profile of the client and determine the scope and nature of your audit procedures.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Risk Description**: Clearly describe each identified risk.\n2. **Likelihood and Impact Assessment**: Evaluate how likely the risk is to occur and its potential impact on the financial statements.\n3. **Related Assertions**: Identify which assertions (e.g., existence, completeness) are affected by the risk.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Overlooking Risks**: Failing to identify all relevant risks can lead to inadequate audit procedures.\n2. **Inaccurate Likelihood and Impact Ratings**: Misjudging these ratings can result in either over- or under-auditing certain areas.\n3. **Ignoring Management’s Input**: Not considering management's views on risks can miss important insights.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form feeds into the **Audit Plan** (Form 520E.1) and **Materiality Analysis** (Form 520E.4). The identified risks help in designing audit procedures that address these areas, ensuring a comprehensive risk assessment process.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nForm 520E.6 satisfies requirements under **ISA 330 – The Auditor’s Responses to Assessed Risks**, which involves identifying and assessing the risks of material misstatement. It also aligns with **ISA 500 – Audit Evid",
    "isaStandards": [],
