    "expertNote": "# Form 670: Journal Entries audit plan\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: it_controls | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 240 | **Connections**: 0 in, 5 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form ID 670: Journal Entries Audit Plan\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm ID 670 is used to plan the testing procedures for journal entries during the audit process. This form helps auditors ensure that all journal entries are properly recorded, accurately reflected, and supported by adequate documentation.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nThis form should be completed during the testing phase of the audit, specifically after the risk assessment and control evaluation phases. It is used when there is a need to verify the completeness, accuracy, and proper authorization of journal entries in the financial statements.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Journal Entries Selection Criteria**: Clearly define how you will select journal entries for testing (e.g., random sampling, specific transactions).\n2. **Testing Procedures**: Outline the steps you will take to test the selected journal entries.\n3. **Evidence Required**: Specify what evidence is needed to support each journal entry (e.g., invoices, memos, approval documents).\n4. **Risk Assessment**: Identify and document any risks associated with the journal entries being tested.\n5. **Reviewers and Timelines**: Assign reviewers for the testing procedures and set deadlines.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Inadequate Selection Criteria**: Not defining clear criteria for selecting journal entries can lead to incomplete or ineffective testing.\n2. **Overlooking Evidence Requirements**: Failing to specify necessary evidence can result in insufficient support for audit conclusions.\n3. **Ignoring Risk Assessment**: Neglecting to assess risks can overlook material misstatements and control weaknesses.\n\n#### Connections:\nThis form is connected to other forms that document the risk assessment, internal controls evaluation, and specific testing results. It feeds int",
