    "expertNote": "# Form EP7: Firm information\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: checklist\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form: EP7 - Firm Information\n\n#### Purpose:\nForm EP7 is used to document key details about the audit client firm. This information is crucial for understanding the context of the audit and ensuring that all necessary steps are taken during the testing phase.\n\n#### When to Complete:\nComplete this form after you have gathered initial information about the client and before diving into detailed testing procedures. It serves as a foundational step in your audit planning process.\n\n#### Key Fields:\n1. **Firm Name and Address**: Ensure these details are accurate to avoid confusion later.\n2. **Industry Classification**: Helps tailor your audit approach based on industry-specific risks.\n3. **Financial Year-End**: Important for scheduling and understanding the timing of financial statements.\n4. **Key Contacts**: Names and roles of key personnel, essential for communication.\n5. **Business Description**: Brief overview to understand the client's operations.\n\n#### Common Mistakes:\n1. **Incorrect or Incomplete Information**: Double-check all details to avoid errors in subsequent steps.\n2. **Ignoring Industry Classification**: Failing to consider industry-specific risks can lead to inadequate audit procedures.\n3. **Overlooking Key Contacts**: Not having accurate contact information can delay the audit process.\n\n#### Connections:\nForm EP7 feeds into other forms like the Risk Assessment (EP1) and Audit Plan (EP2). The information collected here is used to identify risks and plan audit procedures effectively.\n\n#### ISA Context:\nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, Form EP7 aligns with ISAs that emphasize the importance of understanding the client and their environment. This form supports the auditor's ability to assess risk and design appropriate audit procedures.\n\nBy carefully completing this form, you ensure a ",
