    "expertNote": "# Form NFF1: Blank flat-form - landscape\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: ISA text Guidance Content | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form NFF1: Blank flat-form - landscape\n\n#### 1. Purpose\nForm NFF1 is a general-purpose worksheet used during the onboarding phase of an audit to capture initial thoughts, notes, and data. It serves as a flexible space for auditors to organize their preliminary observations and prepare for more detailed work.\n\n#### 2. When to Complete\nYou should complete this form early in the audit process, typically after your initial meetings with client management or when you start gathering basic information about the client's operations. Use it whenever you need a blank sheet to jot down ideas, summarize findings, or plan next steps.\n\n#### 3. Key Fields\n- **Client Name and Contact Information**: Ensure these are accurate for reference throughout the audit.\n- **Date of Entry**: Helps track when specific notes were made, which is crucial for maintaining an audit trail.\n- **Notes/Comments**: This field is critical; it’s where you document your initial thoughts, observations, or questions that need to be addressed.\n\n#### 4. Common Mistakes\n- **Ignoring the Date Field**: Forgetting to enter the date can make it difficult to track when information was recorded.\n- **Poor Organization**: Not organizing notes clearly can lead to confusion later in the audit process.\n- **Overlooking Client Details**: Missing key contact information or client details can hinder communication and follow-up.\n\n#### 5. Connections\nForm NFF1 often feeds into more detailed forms like engagement letters (NFF2) or risk assessments (NFF3). It serves as a starting point for documenting initial impressions, which are then expanded upon in subsequent audit procedures.\n\n#### 6. ISA Context\nThis form supports several ISAs by providing a structured way to capture and document preliminary information:\n- **I",
