    "expertNote": "# Form NWPG: New Work Program\n\n**Phase**: 2_planning | **Category**: general | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 2 out\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of CaseWare Audit Form: New Work Program (NWPG)\n\n#### 1. Purpose:\nThe New Work Program (NWPG) form is used to outline the audit procedures that will be performed during an engagement. It helps auditors plan and document their work efficiently, ensuring all necessary steps are covered.\n\n#### 2. When to Complete:\nYou should complete this form during the planning phase of the audit, typically after you have reviewed the previous year's audit file and identified key areas for focus based on risk assessment.\n\n#### 3. Key Fields:\n- **Audit Procedures**: Clearly describe each procedure you plan to perform.\n- **Objectives**: State what you aim to achieve with each procedure (e.g., verify existence, completeness).\n- **Evidence Required**: Specify the type of evidence needed to support your conclusions.\n- **Responsibility**: Assign who will perform each task.\n- **Timing**: Indicate when each procedure should be completed.\n\n#### 4. Common Mistakes:\n- **Omitting Objectives**: Forgetting to specify what you aim to achieve with each audit step can lead to incomplete or ineffective work.\n- **Lack of Detail in Evidence Required**: Not specifying the type of evidence needed can result in insufficient documentation and support for your conclusions.\n- **Overlooking Timing**: Failing to schedule procedures appropriately can delay the entire audit process.\n\n#### 5. Connections:\nThis form feeds into other audit forms like the Engagement Letter (EL) and the Audit Program Review (APR). It also depends on information from the Risk Assessment (RA) form, which helps identify areas that need more detailed auditing.\n\n#### 6. ISA Context:\nThe NWPG satisfies requirements under **ISA 330: Planning an Audit of Financial Statements** by ensuring a comprehensive audit plan is developed and documented. It also aligns with **IS",
