    "expertNote": "# Form PAY: Payroll Cycle\n\n**Phase**: Substantive Testing & Evidence Gathering | **Category**: Payroll Cycle | **Type**: Leadsheet\n**ISA References**: N/A\n**Connections**: 0 incoming, 0 outgoing | **Procedures**: 0\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\nThis leadsheet provides the summary schedule for Payroll Cycle, consolidating all sub-accounts into a single view that ties to the trial balance and financial statements. It serves as the central navigation point for all detailed testing work in this area.\n\n## When to Complete\nDuring main fieldwork — the core evidence-gathering phase.\n\n## Key Fields to Complete Carefully\n- Opening balance (prior year audited)\n- Current year balance per trial balance\n- Adjusting entries\n- Closing balance per financial statements\n- Variance analysis (year-over-year movement)\n\n## Common Mistakes\n1. Not reconciling the leadsheet to the trial balance before starting detailed work\n2. Failing to investigate material movements from prior year\n3. Not updating the leadsheet for late adjustments or reclassifications\n\n## Connections to Other Forms\nThis form has minimal direct connections but contributes to the overall audit file completeness.\n\n## ISA Context\nNo specific ISA references are tagged to this form, but it supports the overall audit documentation requirements under ISA 230.\n\n## Risk Considerations\n**Primary risks in this area**: Completeness of liabilities, accuracy of calculations, existence of employees (ghost employees)\n",
