    "expertNote": "# Form PMSD: Partner and Manager Summary\n\n**Phase**: Completion & Reporting | **Category**: General / Cross-Cutting | **Type**: Report\n**ISA References**: N/A\n**Connections**: 0 incoming, 0 outgoing | **Procedures**: 0\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\nThis report consolidates and presents the analysis for General / Cross-Cutting, providing a structured summary of findings, conclusions, and matters for attention.\n\n## When to Complete\nAfter fieldwork, before signing the audit report.\nThe report should be drafted during the relevant phase and finalized before moving to the next phase.\n\n## Key Fields to Complete Carefully\n- Executive summary\n- Detailed findings\n- Risk assessment conclusions\n- Recommended actions or further procedures\n\n## Common Mistakes\n1. Not updating the report for changes discovered during later audit phases\n2. Failing to clearly link findings to specific ISA requirements\n3. Omitting significant matters that should be communicated to those charged with governance\n\n## Connections to Other Forms\nThis form has minimal direct connections but contributes to the overall audit file completeness.\n\n## ISA Context\nNo specific ISA references are tagged to this form, but it supports the overall audit documentation requirements under ISA 230.\n\n## Risk Considerations\n**Primary risks in this area**: Varies by specific form — may span multiple audit areas\n",
