    "expertNote": "# Form Q: CaseWare Q - Key Data for Engagements\n\n**Phase**: 1_onboarding | **Category**: general | **Type**: worksheet\n**ISA**: N/A | **Connections**: 0 in, 0 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Q - Key Data for Engagements\n\n**Purpose**:  \nThe CaseWare Q form is used to capture essential information about the audit engagement right from the start. This data helps set the foundation for the entire audit process by providing a clear overview of key details.\n\n**When to Complete**:  \nYou should complete this form during the onboarding phase, typically at the very beginning of an audit engagement, before any substantive work has started. It’s crucial to gather all necessary information as soon as you are assigned to the client.\n\n**Key Fields**:  \n1. **Client Information**: Ensure you have the correct name and address.\n2. **Engagement Type**: Clearly specify whether it's a financial statement audit, review, or other type of engagement.\n3. **Reporting Period**: Enter the start and end dates of the reporting period to avoid confusion later.\n4. **Audit Team Members**: List all team members involved in the engagement.\n5. **Risk Assessment Factors**: Identify any initial risk factors that might affect the audit.\n\n**Common Mistakes**:  \n1. **Incorrect Client Details**: Entering wrong names or addresses can lead to significant issues down the line.\n2. **Omitting Risk Factors**: Failing to identify potential risks early on can result in overlooking critical areas during the audit.\n3. **Incomplete Team Information**: Not listing all team members can cause confusion and affect communication within the audit team.\n\n**Connections**:  \nThis form is foundational and feeds into other forms throughout the audit process. For example, the client information and engagement type from this form are used to populate subsequent forms related to planning and risk assessment.\n\n**ISA Context**:  \nWhile no specific ISA references are listed, the CaseWare Q form aligns with ISAs that require gathering initial in",
