    "expertNote": "# Form SAP: Substantive analytical procedures\n\n**Phase**: Substantive Testing & Evidence Gathering | **Category**: General / Cross-Cutting | **Type**: Procedure\n**ISA References**: ISA 330, ISA 500\n**Connections**: 0 incoming, 0 outgoing | **Procedures**: 3\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\nThis procedure form guides the auditor through the specific audit steps required for General / Cross-Cutting, ensuring ISA compliance and completeness of testing.\n\n## When to Complete\nDuring main fieldwork — the core evidence-gathering phase.\n\n## Key Fields to Complete Carefully\n- Procedure performed (description)\n- Sample size and selection method\n- Results and exceptions\n- Conclusion\n- Reviewer sign-off\n\n## Common Mistakes\n1. Performing procedures mechanically without applying professional skepticism\n2. Not documenting the basis for sample selection\n3. Failing to follow up on exceptions or anomalies found during testing\n\n## Connections to Other Forms\nThis form has minimal direct connections but contributes to the overall audit file completeness.\n\n## ISA Context\nThis form addresses requirements from: ISA 330, ISA 500.\nNon-compliance with these standards may result in an incomplete audit file and potential regulatory findings during practice review.\n\n## Risk Considerations\n**Primary risks in this area**: Varies by specific form — may span multiple audit areas\n",
