    "expertNote": "# Form SPT: Sampling Tool\n\n**Phase**: 4_testing | **Category**: general | **Type**: procedure\n**ISA**: ISA 330, ISA 500 | **Connections**: 0 in, 3 out\n\n---\n\n### CaseWare Audit Form: Sampling Tool (SPT)\n\n**Purpose:**  \nThe Sampling Tool (SPT) helps auditors select a representative sample of transactions or items for testing during the audit process. This ensures that the auditor can make reliable conclusions about the entire population based on the tested sample.\n\n**When to Complete:**  \nYou should complete this form when you need to perform sampling as part of your substantive tests of details in the audit phase. Typically, this occurs after planning and risk assessment, when specific procedures are designed to test controls or transactions.\n\n**Key Fields:**\n1. **Population Description**: Clearly define what population is being sampled (e.g., all sales invoices for Q4).\n2. **Sampling Method**: Choose an appropriate sampling method (e.g., random selection, systematic sampling).\n3. **Sample Size**: Determine the number of items to be tested based on risk assessment and materiality.\n4. **Selection Criteria**: Specify how items are selected from the population (e.g., every 10th invoice).\n5. **Evaluation Criteria**: Outline what criteria will be used to evaluate each sampled item.\n\n**Common Mistakes:**\n1. **Poorly Defined Population**: Not clearly defining the population can lead to incorrect sampling and flawed conclusions.\n2. **Incorrect Sample Size**: Choosing a sample size that is too small may not provide sufficient evidence, while an overly large sample can be inefficient.\n3. **Improper Selection Criteria**: Using inconsistent or biased criteria for selecting items can skew results.\n\n**Connections:**\nThe Sampling Tool form often feeds into other forms such as the Test of Details (TOD) and Audit Program (AP). It provides the basis for which specific transactions are tested, and its results contribute to the overall audit evidence gathered.\n\n**ISA Context:**\nThis for",
